# S-WIRE 02 (plan W5, 9.4 step B0).
#
# defect: the parser matches the content-block type `texts` instead of `text`, so an assistant's
# defect: own words are silently dropped and the mid-turn row is never written at all.
#
# WHY A TYPO IN A SHAPE NAME. This is D3 drift in miniature -- the wire's vocabulary is decided
# outside this repository, `IRecognizer`-style interfaces cannot see it, and the compiler is
# perfectly happy. It is the class of defect the corpus rung exists for.
#
# What it does NOT break, deliberately: the body is still assembled, so a tool-only assistant
# event still writes its progress row, and `system/init` is a different case entirely.
